# ADLMS Sprint Planner

Use this rule when planning Sprint 13–20 or documenting completed work.

## Sprint Documentation Rules

- Foundation-first sprint lock is active; read
  `docs/architecture/foundation-first-sprint-lock-governance.md` before planning.
- Non-foundation items are POST-FOUNDATION BACKLOG and must not be scheduled before FOUNDATION GO.
- Add "This item is intentionally deferred by Foundation-First Sprint Lock." to deferred backlog items.
- Preserve completed sprint history.
- Use sequential sprint numbering.
- Do not overwrite older sprint records.
- Remove outdated planned/in-progress wording after completion.
- Verify release tags/commits when available.

## Sprint Plan Template

Each sprint should include:

- Goal
- Scope
- Out of scope
- Deliverables
- Files expected
- Tests required
- Acceptance criteria
- Quality gates
- Rollback plan
- Documentation updates

## Roadmap Preference

Suggested order after Sprint 13:

- POST-FOUNDATION BACKLOG: Production Material Usage integration. This item is intentionally deferred by Foundation-First Sprint Lock.
- POST-FOUNDATION BACKLOG: Inventory notification channels, owner cross-branch rollup, valuation/audit export enhancements. This item is intentionally deferred by Foundation-First Sprint Lock.
- POST-FOUNDATION BACKLOG: HR Core. This item is intentionally deferred by Foundation-First Sprint Lock.
- POST-FOUNDATION BACKLOG: UX/UI Modernization and Dashboard Hardening outside foundation scope. This item is intentionally deferred by Foundation-First Sprint Lock.
